---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import { appointmentUrl } from '../../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="How Coaching Works | Signal & Structure Coaching"
  description="Learn what to expect from ADHD and executive-function coaching with Signal & Structure Coaching."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The process"
    title="How coaching works"
    intro="A practical process for identifying friction, building useful systems, and adjusting them as real life changes."
    crumbs={[{ label: 'How Coaching Works' }]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with what is actually happening</p>
        <h2>We are not trying to build a perfect routine.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="measure">
        <p class="lead">
          Coaching starts by looking closely at where things break down in real
          life. Maybe the problem is starting, remembering, estimating time,
          switching tasks, deciding what matters first, or recovering after an
          interrupted week.
        </p>
        <p>
          Once the friction is visible, we can design support around it instead
          of relying on more willpower, more reminders, or another system that
          only works when life is unusually calm.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The coaching loop</p>
        <h2>Observe. Decide. Design. Adjust.</h2>
        <p>
          The process is collaborative and practical. Each step gives us more
          useful information about what your system actually needs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process-grid">
        <li>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Observe</h3>
          <p>
            Identify where a task, deadline, routine, or decision begins to
            lose traction.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Decide</h3>
          <p>
            Clarify what matters most right now and choose a manageable problem
            to work on first.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Design</h3>
          <p>
            Build a visible support, routine, cue, planning method, or workflow
            that reduces friction.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Adjust</h3>
          <p>
            Test it during an ordinary week, keep what helps, and change what
            does not hold up.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container session-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Inside a session</p>
        <h2>Come with the real version of the problem.</h2>
        <p>
          You do not need to organize everything before a coaching session.
          Bring the overdue project, the chaotic calendar, the routine that
          disappeared, or the task you keep avoiding.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="session-panel">
        <p class="panel-label">A session may include</p>
        <ul>
          <li>mapping where a task is getting stuck</li>
          <li>breaking a vague goal into visible next actions</li>
          <li>building a planning or capture system</li>
          <li>reducing unnecessary decisions</li>
          <li>creating cues for transitions or task initiation</li>
          <li>reviewing what worked since the last session</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container support-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Scope of coaching</p>
        <h2>Coaching focuses on action, structure, and follow-through.</h2>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p>
          Signal &amp; Structure coaching can support planning, prioritization,
          organization, task initiation, time awareness, routines,
          communication, and practical systems for school or work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Coaching is not psychotherapy, medical treatment, diagnosis, or
          emergency support. When a need falls outside coaching, a licensed
          healthcare or mental-health professional may be the more appropriate
          resource.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container next-step">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A simple starting point</p>
        <h2>You do not have to know what system you need yet.</h2>
        <p>
          A discovery call is a place to talk about what feels difficult,
          what you have already tried, and whether coaching seems like a useful
          next step.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Button href={appointmentUrl} tracking="request-appointment">
        Book a discovery call
      </Button>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intro-grid,
  .session-grid,
  .support-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.6vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .section-heading {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .process-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .process-grid li {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 15rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sand);
    background: white;
  }

  .process-grid li > span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: var(--structure);
    font-size: .7rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .process-grid li:after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 1.5rem;
    right: 1.5rem;
    width: 1rem;
    height: 1rem;
    background: var(--signal);
  }

  .process-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: .65rem;
  }

  .session-panel {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border-left: .35rem solid var(--structure);
    background: #edeee8;
  }

  .panel-label {
    color: var(--signal-text);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: .14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .session-panel ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: .75rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .session-panel li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .session-panel li:before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: .65em;
    left: 0;
    width: .55rem;
    height: .55rem;
    background: var(--signal-strong);
  }

  .next-step {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--sand);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  @media (min-width:48rem) {
    .intro-grid,
    .session-grid,
    .support-grid {
      grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr;
      gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    }

    .process-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .next-step {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width:70rem) {
    .process-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
